  "settingSources": {
    "crFromSiaf": "Paper III.2: the LWB narrow uncal headers carry wrong CRPIX; the mask position is taken from SIAF (spaceKLIP #182, in the pinned commit).",
    "stage1": "Paper III.2: dark subtraction skipped, 4 pseudo-reference pixels on each edge, jump threshold 4. The saturation growth and the three- and four-group thresholds are not in the paper; they are the values of Balmer's own spaceKLIP script of the same period, github.com/wbalmer/aflepb_nircam_ddt aflep_nircam_epoch1_reduction.py.",
    "stage2": "Balmer's AF Lep b script: outlier detection run. The paper does not state it.",
    "badPixels": "Paper III.2: bad pixels the pipeline missed are sigma-clipped at 5. The method chain and its other arguments are Balmer's AF Lep b script (which clips at 3).",
    "padPixels": "Paper III.2: the 400x256 subarray padded to 451x451 ([left, right, bottom, top]).",
    "cropPixels": "Paper III.2: cropped from 451x451 to 201x201.",
    "spectralType": "SIMBAD F0+VkA5mA5 (Gray et al. 2003), as the webbpsf model spectrum for centring; the paper names no type.",
    "align": "Paper III.2: the central leakage masked with a rectangle of zeros and the square root taken for the shift estimate (spaceKLIP #183). The rectangle size is not given; msk_shp 8 is spaceKLIP's default.",
    "blur": "Paper III.2: Gaussian blur FWHM = lambda / 2.3 D with D = 5.2 m before any interpolation; spaceKLIP blur_frames(fact='auto') computes exactly this.",
    "klip": "Paper III.3: the four planets detected with annuli 1, subsections 1, reference-star (RDI) subtraction; ADI+RDI self-subtracts planet e. The KL mode list is ours; the paper prints numbasis > 1."
  },
